course: dictionary
lesson: 14174
title: The Mojave
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The Mojave is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. It can name a place or a group of people. Read the words around it to find out which.
explain: «The Mojave Desert is hot and dry.» Desert tells you it is a place with very little rain. The Mojave is the name of that desert, in the south-west of the USA.
explain: «The Mojave people have lived by the Colorado River for a long time.» Here Mojave names a group of people, not a place. The clues are «people» and «lived».
fact: The Mojave Desert is a hot, dry desert in the south-west of the USA.
fact: Most of the Mojave Desert is in California and Nevada.
fact: Death Valley, one of the hottest places on Earth, is in the Mojave Desert.
fact: The Mojave people are a Native American people who live along the Colorado River.
fact: Mojave is also spelled Mohave.
exercise: «The Mojave Desert is hot and dry.» In this sentence, what is the Mojave? | A river that flows to the sea | A group of people who sing | *A desert, a hot and dry place | A town full of tall buildings
exercise: «The Mojave people have lived by the Colorado River for a long time.» Here, what does Mojave mean? | A cold mountain range | A tall tree with spiky leaves | A large city in Europe | *A Native American people
exercise: «Death Valley, one of the hottest places on Earth, is in the Mojave.» Which place is Death Valley in? | The Alps | *The Mojave Desert | The Sahara in Africa | The Amazon rainforest
test: «The Mojave is hot, dry and mostly in California and Nevada.» Is the Mojave a place or a people? | *A place | Both at once, with no clue | A people | A river
test: «The Mojave people farm the land beside the Colorado River.» What clue tells you Mojave means people? | The word «hot» | The word «river» | The word «desert» | *The word «people»
exam: «The Mojave Desert is in the USA, and the Mojave people live by the Colorado River.» Which word in this sentence tells you the first Mojave is a place? | Colorado | Lived | People | *Desert
